    "narrative": "The cornerstone of today\u2019s offensive attack is **Cal Raleigh** (72.49), whose position behind the plate and high-ceiling matchup against Gage Jump position him as our elite anchor. He is closely trailed by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (69.95) and **Bryce Harper** (65.59), both of whom are clear starts despite facing a respectable arm in Tyler Mahle. The matchup against Mahle is particularly interesting; while he presents a challenge, the projected order placement for **Bryce Harper**, **Luis Arraez**, and **Justin Crawford** creates a volume play that keeps their efficiency scores firmly in the green. We are also capitalizing on high-ceiling leverage with **Kyle Karros** (63.84) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (64.27), the latter of whom benefits significantly from wind conditions, which effectively offset the hurdle of facing a quality arm like Michael King.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Dylan Beavers** (49.94), who sits just outside the active roster despite a strong projected score and a prime spot in the batting order. While **Dylan Beavers** offered legitimate upside, the overall efficiency of the outfield core\u2014specifically the combined platoon and park-adjusted value of **Lawrence Butler** (58.13) and **JJ Bleday** (55.42)\u2014pushed him to the bench to preserve our game caps. We are also exercising caution with **Yainer Diaz** (42.85), who remains active but carries a lowered score due to the matchup against I. Seymour; he is currently flirting with our floor, and any further degradation in his projected order would force a pivot.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for several key assets, including **Cal Raleigh**, **Zack Gelof**, **Luis Arraez**, **Bryce Harper**, **Justin Crawford**, and **Lawrence Butler**. Should official lineups move any of these players down the order, their efficiency scores will suffer, potentially forcing us to utilize high-upside reserves like **Masyn Winn** (43.50). We are holding **Daulton Varsho** (36.27) and **Braden Montgomery** (37.79) firmly on the bench, as their current projections fall below the 40.0 efficiency floor required to risk a game cap usage. With stolen bases at a premium, we are monitoring all baserunning opportunities closely, particularly for those players facing pitchers with slower deliveries.",
